    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2455" contextRef="c-58">&lt;div&gt;&lt;h1 style="margin: 6pt 0 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION AND OPERATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Organization. &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;ETC Tiger Pipeline, LLC (&amp;quot;Tiger&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Operations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. Tiger is primarily engaged in the interstate transportation of natural gas and as such, Tiger is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;).Tiger owns and operates approximately 197 miles of interstate natural gas pipeline that originates in Panola County, Texas, and continues eastward to the heart of the Haynesville Shale and ends near Delhi, Louisiana with interconnects to several interstate pipelines at various points in Louisiana. The pipeline has capacity to transport up to 2.4 billion cubic feet per day. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger evaluated subsequent events through April 7, 2026, the date on which the accompanying financial statements were available to be issued. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly recognized and/or disclosed in these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h1 style="margin: 6pt 0 0; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE B - ESTIMATES AND SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;1.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger's financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and statement of cash flows and (2) certain assets and liabilities from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;2.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Although these estimates are based on management's available knowledge of current and expected future events, actual results could differ from those estimates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;3.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger has a cash management agreement with Energy Transfer which authorizes Energy Transfer or its designated affiliate to provide cash management services to Tiger. At the close of each business day, the agreement allows for Tiger to transfer funds in excess of general operating purposes to Energy Transfer or if Tiger has insufficient funds to meet its general operating purposes, Energy Transfer will transfer all funds necessary to Tiger. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;4.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant materials and operating supplies are carried at the lower of weighted average cost or net realizable value. Materials transferred out of warehouses are priced at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;5.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;N&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;atural Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances occur as a result of differences in volumes of natural gas received and delivered. Tiger records natural gas imbalance in-kind receivables and payables at the current market index and dollar valued imbalances at contractual prices with no impact on revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;6.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas Owed to System Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger accounts for Gas owed to system gas, Account 117.4, using the fixed asset accounting model established under FERC Order No. 581. Under this approach, gas owed to system gas volumes are classified as fixed assets and valued at historical cost. Encroachments upon gas owed to system gas are valued at current market prices. Tiger may sell gas owed to system gas in excess of its system operational requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;7.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Fuel Tracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The fuel tracker is the cumulative balance of compressor fuel volumes owed to Tiger by its customers or owed by Tiger to its customers for gas used in the operation of its system, including fuel gas, lost and unaccounted for gas and booster compression fuel. The fuel gas reimbursement percentage is based on specified percentages pursuant to Tiger's tariff in order to recover gas used in the operation of its system. The net difference between the fuel reimbursement percentage received and gas used in the operation of its system is valued at the East TX North LA Carthage Hub Average Monthly Index Rate and recorded in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, or Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, as applicable. Semi-annually, in June and December, the fuel gas reimbursement will be adjusted pursuant to the tariff. The fuel reimbursement is in-kind and non-discountable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Tiger's fuel tracker has a balance of $0.9 million and $1.0 million in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3 and in Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;8.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Additions&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. Ongoing additions of utility plant are stated at original cost. Tiger capitalizes all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. Such indirect construction costs primarily include labor and related costs of departments associated with supporting construction activities and allowance for funds used during construction. The indirect capitalized labor and related costs are largely based upon results of periodic time studies or management reviews of time allocations, which provide an estimate of time spent supporting construction projects. The cost of replacements and betterments that extend the useful life of utility plant is also capitalized. The cost of repairs and replacements of minor utility plant items is charged to expense as incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Retirements. &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When ordinary retirements of utility plant occur, the original cost plus cost of removal less salvage value, is removed by a charge to accumulated depreciation and amortization, with no gain or loss recorded. When entire regulated operating units of utility plant are sold, the original cost and related accumulated depreciation and amortization accounts are removed, with any resulting gain or loss recorded in the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Depreciation&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger computed depreciation expense under the composite method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. For general and intangible plant, Tiger computed depreciation expense under the straight-line method using FERC-approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger capitalizes the cost of funds used during construction for capital projects. The rates used by Tiger are calculated pursuant to the FERC rules, which include an allowance for the cost of debt and equity funds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;9.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. Tiger did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as a part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense or regulatory asset, as applicable, with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability. Tiger was not able to reasonably measure the fair value of the AROs as of December 31, 2025 or 2024 as the expected settlement dates were indeterminable. Tiger will record an ARO in the periods in which Tiger can reasonably determine the settlement dates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;10.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include revenues earned from and payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.Transactions are generally allocated based on relevant criteria, including time spent, utility plant, gross margin, salaries, or other appropriate methods. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;11.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable and the costs can be reasonably estimated. Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;12.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger's revenues from transportation of natural gas are based on capacity reservation charges and, to a lesser extent, commodity usage charges. Reservation revenues, recognized monthly, are based on contracted rates and capacity reserved by the customers. Revenues from commodity usage charges, also recognized monthly, are based on the volumes received from or delivered to the customer, based on Tiger's tariff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Revenues collected during the pendency of a rate proceeding may be required by the FERC to be refunded in the final order. Tiger establishes reserves for such potential refunds, as appropriate. No such reserves were required as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 12pt 0 12pt 0.25in; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span&gt;13.&lt;span style="font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Expected Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger has a large number of customers that are natural gas producers. The large number of customers in this energy segment may impact Tiger's overall exposure to credit risk, either positively or negatively, in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic or other conditions. Tiger manages credit risk to mitigate credit losses and exposure to uncollectible trade receivables. Prospective and existing customers are reviewed regularly for creditworthiness based upon pre-established standards consistent with FERC filed tariffs to manage credit risk within approved tolerances. Customers that do not meet minimum credit standards are required to provide additional credit support in the form of a letter of credit, prepayment, or other forms of security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Tiger establishes an allowance for expected credit losses on trade receivables based on the expected ultimate recovery of these receivables and considers many factors including historical customer collection experience, general and specific economic trends and known specific issues related to individual customers, sectors and transactions that might impact collectability. Changes in the allowance are recorded as a component of operating expenses; reductions in the allowance are recorded when receivables are subsequently collected or written-off. Past due receivable balances are written-off when Tiger's efforts have been unsuccessful in collecting the amount due. Tiger's allowance for expected credit losses was immaterial as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table presents the relative contribution to Tiger's total transportation revenues from operations of each customer that comprised at least 10% of its revenues:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="379" style="width: 284.05pt; margin-left: 67.5pt" class="e-rte-paste-table"&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 15.6pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="140" style="width: 104.65pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 15.6pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="21" style="width: 15.65pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 15.6pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="218" colspan="3" style="width: 163.75pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 15.6pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;Years Ended December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;  &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 14.9pt"&gt;   &lt;td width="140" style="width: 104.65pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.9pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="21" style="width: 15.65pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.9pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;   &lt;td width="99" style="width: 74.15pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 14.9pt"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &l